ream":"zero: preserve paired and aliased fields when using keep_fields (#7069) (#7077)\n\n## Problem\nWhen using the `zero` plugin in whitelist mode (`keep_fields`), paired\nand aliased fields in `MediaFile` (such as `genre` and `genres`,\n`artist` and `artists`, etc.) were not treated as aliases. If a user\nspecified `keep_fields: [genres]`, the singular `genre` field was not in\nthe keep set and was queued to be nulled. Writing `genre = None` to the\nunderlying `MediaFile` wiped out the genre metadata on disk.\nSymmetrically, specifying `genre` in `keep_fields` resulted in `genres`\nbeing zeroed, as reported in #7069.\n\n## Solution\n- Define `FIELD_ALIASES` in `beetsplug/zero.py` containing groups of\npaired and aliased fields (`images`/`art`, `genre`/`genres`,\n`artist`/`artists`, `albumartist`/`albumartists`, etc.).\n- When constructing the whitelist `keep` set, expand it to include all\nmembers of any alias group for which at least one member is listed in\n`keep_fields`.\n- Added regression tests in `test/plugins/test_zero.py` verifying that\nspecifying `art`, `genre`, `genres`, or `artist` in `keep_fields`\npreserves the metadata on disk.\n- Added changelog entry in `docs/changelog.rst`.\n\nFixes #7069.","upstream_url":"https://github.com/beetbox/beets/commit/458390ea297496ea7f0a8629e5453dee59b722d9"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","BEETSDIR=/config","EDITOR=nano"],"exposed_ports":["8337/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-458390ea-ls25.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-458390ea-ls25/diff.json